<%- include('../partials/layout-start') %>
<%- include('../partials/page-header', {
  icon: 'bi-envelope',
  heading: 'Contact us',
  sub: 'A person reads these.'
}) %>
<section class="glass-section pb-5">
<div class="container">
  <div class="row justify-content-center"><div class="col-lg-8">
    <div class="glass-card mb-4"><div class="card-body">
      <h2 class="h5">Email</h2>
      <p class="mb-3">
        <a class="fs-5" href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a>
      </p>
      <%#
        There is a form below now. It shipped as an address alone until all three of the
        things that note demanded existed: somewhere to put what it collects (migration
        018), a spam defence (a rate limit, a honeypot and a length floor) and somebody
        watching a queue (/admin/enquiries). The address stays, because somebody writing
        from their own client has a copy of what they sent and a form gives them nothing.
      %>
      <p class="text-muted-2 mb-0">
        We answer during UK working hours. Please include your account email if your
        question is about something on your account — we cannot look anybody up from a
        name alone.
      </p>
    </div></div>

    <div class="glass-card mb-4"><div class="card-body">
      <h2 class="h5">What to tell us</h2>
      <ul class="mb-0">
        <li><strong>A payment or an invoice</strong> — the payment reference from
            <a href="/payments/history">your payments page</a>. It starts with <code>PAY-</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>A quote</strong> — the quote reference, which starts with <code>Q-</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>A job or an application</strong> — the link to the advert.</li>
        <li><strong>Something that looks wrong on the site</strong> — the page you were on and
            what you expected to happen.</li>
        <li><strong>Your data, or closing your account</strong> — say so plainly and we will
            handle it under the <a href="/legal/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</li>
      </ul>
    </div></div>

    <div class="glass-card mb-4"><div class="card-body">
      <h2 class="h5">Or write here</h2>
      <% if (errors.length) { %>
        <div class="alert alert-danger">
          <ul class="mb-0">
            <% errors.forEach(function (e) { %><li><%= e.msg %></li><% }) %>
          </ul>
        </div>
      <% } %>
      <form method="post" action="/contact">
        <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
        <%- include('../partials/enquiry-fields', { values }) %>
        <button class="btn btn-primary mt-3" type="submit">Send message</button>
      </form>
    </div></div>

    <div class="glass-card"><div class="card-body">
      <h2 class="h5">Before you write</h2>
      <p class="mb-0 text-muted-2">
        Prices are on the <a href="/payments">pricing page</a>, how the day-rate index is
        built is explained on <a href="/rates">the index itself</a>, and what the estimator
        does with your inputs is on <a href="/quotes/new">the estimator</a>.<% if (assistantReady) { %>
        The assistant in the corner of the page answers questions about how the Hub works —
        though it cannot see your account, so anything account-specific still comes here.<% } %>
      </p>
    </div></div>
  </div></div>
</div>
</section>
<%- include('../partials/layout-end') %>
